  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Importing recycled PET</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Europe is a strong growing demand for recycled PET (transparent plastics mostly used for bottles and packaging) of a certain quality. In Asian and Africa countries, more specific Indonesia, Bangladesh and South Africa, there is a strong growth of consumption in PET, therefore growing volume of plastic waste. A strong local demand for the waste RPET is absent which creates a business opportunity in exporting RPET to Europe. DGGF TA helped pre-finance 7 containers of PET waste from Indonesia, Bangladesh and South Africa. The import of PET has led to a lot of supported indirect jobs in the countries, both at the factories where PET is being sorted and processed, but also among waste collectors. These specific shippings have led to 45 FTE. During the course of the project approximately 600 people have been trained on what plastics to collect, sorting of materials, using machinery and cleaning of the products. As a result of the project, the recycling industry in developing countries will be strengthened and CO2 emissions in Europe diminish, as recycled PET needs far less energy compared to virgin PET.</narrative>
  </description>
